Package: kblocker
Version: 1.0-1
Architecture: ARCH
Maintainer: kblocker maintainer <root@localhost>
Depends: dkms, gnupg, e2fsprogs, xxd, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0
Recommends: perl, pkexec | policykit-1
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: Self-discipline internet blocker kernel module
 kblocker is a Linux kernel module that blocks network access
 to user-configured domains and IPs for a time-limited period.
 .
 Designed as a focus tool: once enabled, it is deliberately
 difficult to disable early. Supports PGP-based key escrow
 so a trusted remote party can authorize unblocking.
 .
 Blocking is disabled by default after installation.
 Use 'kblockerctl enable <minutes>' to activate, or run
 'sudo kblocker' for the desktop app.
